{"type":"standard","title":"Jocelyn Benson","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Jocelyn Benson</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q13562375","titles":{"canonical":"Jocelyn_Benson","normalized":"Jocelyn Benson","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Jocelyn Benson</span></span>"},"pageid":22433126,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/SOS_Jocelyn_Benson_web.jpg/330px-SOS_Jocelyn_Benson_web.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":397},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/57/SOS_Jocelyn_Benson_web.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":2660,"height":3202},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1376210949","tid":"2cfcc3cb-b6be-11f1-8b6b-7da69eaf03a2","timestamp":"2026-09-22T19:45:34Z","description":"American politician and attorney (born 1977)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jocelyn_Benson","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jocelyn_Benson?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jocelyn_Benson?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Jocelyn_Benson"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jocelyn_Benson","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Jocelyn_Benson","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jocelyn_Benson?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Jocelyn_Benson"}},"extract":"Jocelyn Michelle Benson is an American politician and attorney who has served as the 43rd secretary of state of Michigan since 2019. A member of the Democratic Party, she served as dean of Wayne State University Law School from 2012 to 2016.","extract_html":"<p><b>Jocelyn Michelle Benson</b> is an American politician and attorney who has served as the 43rd secretary of state of Michigan since 2019. A member of the Democratic Party, she served as dean of Wayne State University Law School from 2012 to 2016.</p>"}